    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d53">

                <pb facs="0170" n="70" sameAs="frus:frus1920v03/pg70"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">882.00/653</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of
                            State to the Secretary of the Navy</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Daniels</hi>)</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1920-06-22"><hi rendition="#italic">June 22,
                        1920</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p rendition="#flush">(Attention of Admiral Coontz, Chief of Naval Operations)</p>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to acknowledge the receipt
                    of your letter of the 11th [<hi rendition="#italic">15th</hi>] instant<anchor
                        n="12" xml:id="d53-f1"/> and to thank you for the paraphrase of a despatch
                    contained therein received by your Department from the Commander of the U.S.S.
                        <hi rendition="#italic">Chattanooga</hi> on conditions in Liberia.</p>
                <p>In view of the serious conditions alleged in this report to exist in Liberia at a
                    moment when we are negotiating an agreement with that Government with a view of
                    improving conditions in Liberia, it is earnestly requested that a small naval
                    vessel make its base at the port of Monrovia for the present.</p>
                <p>I have [etc.]</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Norman H. Davis</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
